Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:39:28 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 16/27] Plutonium: network access from the shell's settings

T3's desktop app switches "Network access" by restarting its backend on
another host. The Plutonium shell is a browser page, so the switch was
disabled ("restart with a non-loopback host"), and other devices and T3
apps couldn't pair with this machine from the UI.

- The server, in a Plutonium session, answers /api/plutonium/network-access:
  GET reports the mode; POST (environment:maintain, JSON only) saves it in
  $T3CODE_HOME/plutonium-network-access and stops the server. Plutonium's
  launcher runs it under a supervisor that starts it again on 0.0.0.0 or
  127.0.0.1. T3_HOST in Plutonium's settings pins the host.
- Settings, Connections in the shell shows the desktop app's switch, its
  confirmation and its LAN endpoints, and waits for the server to return.
- The session cookie keeps its loopback name on either host, so the shell
  stays signed in across the switch.

